<title>SWITZERLAND: Nokia's Maillefer 1996 profits slump.</title>
<headline>Nokia's Maillefer 1996 profits slump.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nokia's Maillefer Holding SA affiliate said on Tuesday that its net profit in 1996 slumped to 2.3 million Swiss Francs from 24.1 million in 1995.</p>
<p>The cable systems producer based in Ecublens, Lausanne, also said it would propose a reduction in the dividend to nine Swiss francs per bearer share from 17.10 francs at its next shareholders meeting on April 29.  </p>
<p>Maillefer Holding SA said its 1996 turnover fell three percent to 317.7 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>The company said markets in eastern and central Europe as well as in southeast Asia were favourable in 1996 but that it suffered from contraction elsewhere. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
